WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:11.120
After writing the paper, comes the time of reading&nbsp;
your paper a few times in order to get everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:15.840
perfect. In this section you will learn how to&nbsp;
remove a lot of mistakes you might have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:21.280
writing. In the end, you will have to build your&nbsp;
own checklist corresponding to your own problems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:26.960
you want to avoid. After this, your article can&nbsp;
be submitted and will hopefully be accepted!!
 &nbsp;

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.120
Let’s discuss the mistakes to&nbsp;
avoid before submitting the paper.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:36.800
Let’s look at content mistakes. When you&nbsp;
are writing something you want to get people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:41.120
interested by the content of your article, by&nbsp;
the science behind it, but you also want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:46.400
maintain an internal coherent. So, you have to&nbsp;
make sure you answer the following questions:
 &nbsp;

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:48.800
Do you pass the so what test?&nbsp;

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:52.800
Does the problem statement remain&nbsp;
the same throughout the paper?&nbsp;

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:57.840
Is the title of the paper coherent?
Are the keywords adequate?&nbsp;

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:03.360
Is the content of your research coherent with the&nbsp;
aims and scopes of the journal you are targeting?
 &nbsp;

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:07.680
The people that are going to read your&nbsp;
article are first the chief editor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:11.840
then specialized editor, then the anonymous&nbsp;
reviewers, and finally your community.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:16.560
Be careful to be coherent and rigorous,&nbsp;
so that they can follow your thinking. 
 &nbsp;

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:23.280
Asking someone else to read your paper once again&nbsp;
is a good idea. He or she will give you his or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:28.160
her views on how to improve the paper itself,&nbsp;
and more importantly, it can detect mistakes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:34.560
This person is going to give you the first set of&nbsp;
tips that one needs before the submission. You can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:39.440
also check that your article is not boring because&nbsp;
then the peer review process will just eliminate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:44.880
this paper. You have to keep in mind that your&nbsp;
writing is going to be evaluated by your peers.&nbsp;

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:50.560
Improper language, spelling mistakes,&nbsp;
typos all these are a no go.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:56.160
You should always be very mindful of your writing&nbsp;
because it can convey the feeling that the paper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:59.520
and the authors are not very rigorous&nbsp;
nor up to the journal's standards.
 &nbsp;

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:04.960
You will want to make sure that everything is&nbsp;
crystal clear, that there is no long sentence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:09.040
that you are always writing in an active&nbsp;
voice for English papers and not a passive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:14.720
one. And there is no need for complicated words,&nbsp;
so just make it simple and straight to the point.
 &nbsp;

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:19.200
If you are like the rest of us, you will&nbsp;
know it’s hard to correct your own paper.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:25.040
So, try and find proofreading buddies.&nbsp;
Some friends who will read your paper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:29.920
and to whom you will return the favor.
 
If English is not your native language,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:35.680
it is always a good idea to use a professional&nbsp;
copy editor. But do it when the final version of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:41.280
the paper is available, because this service&nbsp;
of language editing is very costly. If you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:45.280
have submission deadlines, don't forget&nbsp;
to take this time factor into account.
 &nbsp;

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:50.640
Then there are some common format oversights,&nbsp;
like forgetting the paper's pagination,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:54.560
something which really frustrates reviewers&nbsp;
since it prevents them from referring to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.560 --> 00:03:00.160
specific page in their comments. Also, watch&nbsp;
out for improper bibliographical styles.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:04.400
Always make sure you know the right&nbsp;
rules for the journal you are targeting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:08.160
And always make sure you are&nbsp;
respecting their citing styles.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:15.200
For that, you can often download a template or the&nbsp;
writing rules on the website or the journal. It is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:19.680
important to follow the words limit and all the&nbsp;
guidelines that you have to comply with regarding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:25.360
the paragraphs, the font and the size and so on.
 
Another important point is the adequate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:30.880
organization of the paper. Make sure you have&nbsp;
clear sections and subsections as well as short&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:36.320
introduction paragraphs or conclusion.&nbsp;
This helps clarify the argumentation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:41.840
and makes it easier for the reader to follow.
 
Also, verify that the titles of sections,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:47.920
of figures and tables, of the paper itself, are&nbsp;
the right ones. That they correspond exactly to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:52.400
what you are showing in the paragraph, in the&nbsp;
table, in the figure, and in the paper itself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:59.840
If you have specific form requirements in your&nbsp;
discipline, make sure you comply with them.&nbsp;

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:05.280
In order to submit the paper, you also have&nbsp;
to write a cover letter, which is a letter to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:11.120
the editor describing what you did, in maximum,&nbsp;
one page. The objective is to convince of your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:16.480
paper's interest. The same basic mistake can&nbsp;
occur in this letter so make sure you write a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:22.160
well-crafted, interesting, and clear letter.
 
In the reviewing process we described before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:25.360
you will then have to write letters to&nbsp;
the reviewers to answer the comments.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:32.320
Always be respectful toward them and mindful of&nbsp;
their opinion, recommendation, or critiques. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:37.520
they don't understand what you wrote, it is&nbsp;
probably because it was not clear enough. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:41.840
here again, if you take care of all the mistakes&nbsp;
that we have defined earlier it should be fine.&nbsp;

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:49.920
In the earlier video on authorship, we&nbsp;
have discussed ICMJE guidelines that help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:55.840
researchers in deciding whether a contributor&nbsp;
qualifies to be an author or not. In this video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.840 --> 00:05:00.320
we are going to discuss the order in which author&nbsp;
names should be included in a multi-author paper.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:05.920
The order of authors on a scientific paper needs&nbsp;
to be determined after careful deliberation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:08.800
Prior to deciding the author order,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:13.040
it is important to understand the concept&nbsp;
of a first and a corresponding author.&nbsp;

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:20.480
Who should be the first author?
The first author is usually the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:24.560
person who has made the most significant&nbsp;
intellectual contribution to the work, in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:30.080
terms designing the study, acquiring and analyzing&nbsp;
data from experiments, and writing the manuscript.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:34.560
The importance of the first author&nbsp;
is reflected in the common practice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:39.040
of referring to a paper by the first&nbsp;
author’s name. Publishing a paper as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:43.440
the first author is very crucial for the&nbsp;
scientific career of a Ph.D. student.
 &nbsp;

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:49.200
After the first author, the subsequent authors are&nbsp;
usually listed as per their contribution to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:55.280
research, starting with the one who contributed&nbsp;
the most to the least. However, sometimes multiple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.280 --> 00:06:00.080
authors may have contributed equally, in which&nbsp;
case the order of author names does not matter.
 &nbsp;

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:06.800
What is the role of a corresponding author?
At the time of submission of a manuscript,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:10.640
journals require you to choose one of&nbsp;
the authors as the corresponding author.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:16.000
The corresponding author is the one who receives&nbsp;
all notifications from the journal including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:21.360
manuscript status, reviewers’ comments,&nbsp;
and the final decision. Although journals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:26.240
usually perceive the role of a corresponding&nbsp;
author as purely administrative, this role is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:32.080
associated with seniority in some cultures. The&nbsp;
corresponding author is often the group leader&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:36.640
or a senior researcher whose contact address&nbsp;
is not likely to change in the near future.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:42.320
In cases where the main contributor of the study&nbsp;
is also the group leader, he or she can be both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:48.720
the first and corresponding author for the study.
 
Gift authorship&nbsp;

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:53.760
For a student who has been left off an author&nbsp;
list, it can be especially maddening to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.760 --> 00:07:00.080
someone included who obviously doesn't deserve it.&nbsp;
Also called "honorary," or "guest," authors, gift&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:05.280
authors don't make a significant contribution (or&nbsp;
sometimes any contribution at all) to the paper.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:10.000
Motivations for gift authorship&nbsp;
vary; the principal investigator&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:14.480
(PI) may think he's doing the recipient a&nbsp;
favor, or she or he may think that adding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:18.800
the name of a well-known scientist will improve&nbsp;
the odds of getting published in a top journal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:24.080
Gift authors can appear anywhere on the author&nbsp;
list, but usually they're listed in the middle.
 &nbsp;

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:30.960
Gift authorship is especially damaging when the&nbsp;
recipient is a senior author. Anyone who doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:35.360
realize that the authorship is honorary will&nbsp;
wrongly assume that this well-known scientist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:41.040
has performed his or her role in ensuring the&nbsp;
integrity of the data. Sometimes authorships are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:48.080
even "gifted" without the recipient's knowledge.
In summary, As you can see, choosing the author&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:53.200
order can be quite complicated; therefore, we&nbsp;
urge researchers to consider these factors early&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:58.000
in the research process and to confirm this order&nbsp;
while editing your manuscript before submission&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:03.520
to journals. Don’t wait until the manuscript is&nbsp;
drafted before you decide on the author order.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:08.640
All the parties involved will need to&nbsp;
agree on the author list before submission,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:12.080
and no one will want to delay submission&nbsp;
because of a disagreement about who should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:17.600
be included on the author list and in what&nbsp;
order. Additionally, we recommend periodically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:22.240
revisiting the named author issue to make sure&nbsp;
that everyone is on the same page and that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:33.920
list is updated to appropriately reflect changes&nbsp;
in team composition or contributions to a work.

